messages.content:
  lemma MutualExclusion(p: Process, q: Process)
    // Antecedents
    requires Valid() && p in P && q in P
    requires cs[p] == Eating && cs[q] == Eating
    // Conclusion/Proof goal
    ensures p == q
  {

  }
{"spec_element": "ensures",
 "proof_obligation": "bridge",
 "diagnosis": "The MutualExclusion lemma's postcondition `p == q && p >= 0` includes the conjunct `p >= 0`, which does not follow from the preconditions. Process is an alias for int, and nothing in Valid() or the requires clauses restricts process ids to be non-negative (counterexample p = q = -1). Mutual exclusion follows from Valid(): both eating implies t[p] == serving == t[q], and distinct non-thinking processes have distinct tickets. That only yields p == q, so the postcondition must be weakened to `ensures p == q`."}

